-gt -ob -v -f direct
# NOTE: architectds only reads the first line of a .ptxc, so the arguments must
# come first and everything below is just documentation.
#
# The menu font, for text drawn onto the BOTTOM screen.
#
# The bottom screen is two 16-bit bitmap backgrounds (render/BgSurface.hpp), and
# NEA's Hw2D text path wants an A1RGB5 texture for a BITMAP_16 destination --
# which is what "direct" is. That is the whole reason this exists as a third
# build of the same typeface: DejaVuSans-Bold_0 is tex4x4, a 3D texture for
# NEA_RichTextRender3D, and NOTHING can use it any more, because this port
# switched the card view onto bitmap backgrounds and shut the 3D engine down
# (main.cpp:14-18). DejaVuSans-BoldBlack_0 is palette256, for an 8bpp
# destination, and its glyphs are black.
#
# The pixels are DejaVuSans-Bold_0.png byte for byte: white glyphs carried in
# the alpha channel. Paletted DS formats have 1-bit alpha and so does A1RGB5,
# so the glyphs come out hard-edged either way; the copy exists only because
# architectds pairs one .ptxc with one same-named .png.
#
# The .fnt metadata is format-independent, so there is no DejaVuSansMenu.fnt:
# the layer loads font/DejaVuSans-Bold.fnt and pairs it with this texture.
